    <h3>ANOMALY T-02: <code>pulse.yml</code> — TRAILING "EOF" ARTIFACT (CRITICAL — UNRESOLVED)</h3>

    <p>
        Line 25 of <code>pulse.yml</code> contains the literal string <code>EOF</code>:
    </p>

    <pre style="background: #111; border: 1px solid #333; padding: 10px; color: #39FF14; overflow-x: auto;">
          python-version: '3.10'
      - name: Install dependencies
        run: pip install requests
      - name: Run Pulse
        run: python3 pulse.py
        env:
          TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN }}
          TELEGRAM_HOME_CHANNEL: ${{ secrets.TELEGRAM_HOME_CHANNEL }}
    EOF</pre>

    <p>
        This is not valid YAML. The string <code>EOF</code> is a heredoc terminator artifact, likely
        copied from a shell script or created by an editor that treated the file as a heredoc
        template. GitHub Actions' YAML parser will fail before reaching the <code>env</code> block,
        meaning the entire workflow may fail to parse. The <code>pulse.py</code> script may never
        execute in the CI environment, even if the Python syntax were corrected.
    </p>

    <p>
        <strong>Resolution:</strong> Delete line 25 (<code>EOF</code>) and verify the YAML parses
        correctly with <code>python3 -c "import yaml; yaml.safe_load(open('pulse.yml'))"</code>.
    </p>

